# What `npm pack` may put in the @nullarch/resin tarball. scripts/package-smoke.mjs fails when a
# packed file matches no line here, and when a line here matches no packed file.
#
# One path per line; `#` starts a comment. `*` matches within a path segment, `**` across segments.
# Regenerate the full list for review with:  node scripts/package-smoke.mjs --list
#
# Anything new that ships is a decision: add it here in the same change that adds it to the
# "files" array of package.json. Tests, corpus, oracle, coverage, docs and examples must never ship
# (package-smoke also refuses them whatever this file says).

# package.json "files" plus what npm always includes (package.json, LICENSE, README.md)
package.json
LICENSE
README.md
README.zh-CN.md
README.ja.md
README.ko.md
API.md
CHANGELOG.md

# the CLI and the plain-Node loader hook (`node --import @nullarch/resin/register`)
bin/resin.mjs
register.mjs
scripts/ts-esm-loader-hook.mjs

# The product: TypeScript source, shipped as is. Pattern rather than 48 lines because the
# modules under src/ come and go with every feature; the .ts restriction still catches a stray
# fixture, JSON dump, snapshot or backup file in there. Today: src/index.ts, src/runtime/*.ts,
# src/transpiler/*.ts, src/transpiler/analyzer/*.ts, src/transpiler/passes/*.ts.
src/**/*.ts
